{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.ExceptionalDivisor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.ExceptionalDivisor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.south_pole_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.south_pole_independent","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/exceptional-divisor.lean#L59-L67","doc":"The exceptional divisor is topologically S² ≅ ℙ¹(ℂ): the full\nparameter range φ ∈ [0, π], ψ ∈ [0, 2π) covers the sphere exactly once.\nThis is encoded by the statement that at the poles (φ = 0 and φ = π),\nthe point is independent of ψ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.fibrePoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.fibrePoint","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/exceptional-divisor.lean#L51-L57","doc":"A point on the exceptional divisor parametrized by spherical\ncoordinates (φ, ψ). Returns the i-th coordinate of the fibre point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.tangent2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.tangent2","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/exceptional-divisor.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Second tangent vector T₂. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.tangent1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.tangent1","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/exceptional-divisor.lean#L47-L47","doc":"First tangent vector T₁. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.normal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.normal","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/exceptional-divisor.lean#L45-L45","doc":"The outward unit normal N(p) at the brane point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.centre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.centre","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/exceptional-divisor.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The centre offset from the brane point along the normal:\nO(p) = p + R · N(p). Here represented as the ℝ³ coordinates\nof the centre. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.R_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.R_pos","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/exceptional-divisor.lean#L39-L39","doc":"Radius is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.R","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.R","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/exceptional-divisor.lean#L37-L37","doc":"The radius of the ℙ¹(ℂ) fibre. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ExceptionalDivisor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/exceptional-divisor.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ExceptionalDivisor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ExceptionalDivisor","kind":"structure","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/exceptional-divisor.lean#L22-L49","doc":"**Exceptional divisor** at a brane point: the ℙ¹(ℂ) fibre obtained\nby blowing up a brane point p ∈ M.  Parametrized by spherical\ncoordinates (φ, ψ) where φ ∈ [0, π] is the polar angle and\nψ ∈ [0, 2π) is the azimuthal angle.\n\nThe fibre point in ℝ³ is given by:\n  𝒮_p(φ, ψ) = O(p) + R(sin φ (cos ψ T₁ + sin ψ T₂) - cos φ N)\n\nwhere O(p) = p + R·N(p) is the centre, N(p) the outward normal,\nand (T₁, T₂) a positively-oriented tangent frame.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:exceptional-divisor}`\nRef: [leitner2026] Chapter 6, §Colour-sector coordinates ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:exceptional-divisor","label":"def:exceptional-divisor","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/exceptional-divisor.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}